- `<F1-SUMMARY>` = [B1052] API wake retry: the retry mark also covers a failed connection close, which would repeat a write if a close ever threw those errors, and code comments say no command was sent (minor; merged in pull request 271, not deployed)
- `<F1-0>` = BLUF: the retry added by pull request 271 (squash d8981b0e00751c69247320085584e0939968043b) marks failures through EF's connection-failed hook (api/src/HpsmPoc.Modules.Assessment/Persistence/SqlServerWakeRetry.cs lines 60-69). EF reports a failed connection close through that same hook (RelationalConnection.cs lines 907-909 and 976-978, EF 10.0.12), so a login timeout or a pool wait thrown by a close inside a retried operation is retried as well. Gate B1052 measured it in process with a forged close failure through the real registration: a non-query sent twice and a SaveChanges insert sent twice, where the previous main threw and sent each once. It cannot happen with the SqlClient this API loads: as the gate read the source of SqlClient 6.1.6, its close path swallows network errors and the pool wait is raised only while getting a connection (no failing close was run against a real SqlClient). A later SqlClient, another provider or a product ConnectionClosing interceptor would make it a repeated write. Graded minor by the gate. Nothing here is deployed.
- `<F1-1>` = False text at main d8981b0e, code comments only: SqlServerWakeRetry.cs line 18 says they are retried only when thrown while opening, no command was sent, so retrying cannot repeat work; lines 38 and 44-45 say the hook means thrown while opening; the same claim sits at lines 31-32 and 48; api/tests/HpsmPoc.Api.Tests/Hosting/SqlServerWakeOpenRetryTests.cs line 27 says no command was sent. The squash message was corrected and states the limit. Fix shape (the gate's): mark only failures raised between ConnectionOpening and ConnectionOpened, for example a per-connection opening flag set in ConnectionOpening(Async) and cleared in ConnectionOpened(Async) and ConnectionClosing(Async), so ConnectionFailed(Async) marks only while the flag is set; prove it with rows in which a close throws (each must fall back to thrown, sent once) plus the 11 existing rows; correct the sentences. Done when: a failure raised by a close is not marked, a row turns red when it is, and the comments state what the code does, or the item is recorded as declined.
- `<F1-2>` = Provenance: gate report B1052 (its close-path section and findings) and builder report B1049, in 1_Project_Definition/Briefs/; the gate's cells are in the B1052 evidence folder, which is not copied to the analysis repository. Decision record: entry {C-271}. Related: HPSMPOC-428, whose code half this follows. Filed by records brief B1055, 2026-11-01. [REC-RES-CLOSEPATH-01NOV-B1055]
- `<F2-SUMMARY>` = [B1052] API wake retry tests: five changes to the retry rule turn none of the 11 new rows red (keyed scope, sync hook, repeated mark, subclass, inner exception) (minor, test-only; merged in pull request 271, not deployed)
- `<F2-0>` = BLUF: gate B1052 planted changes in the retry added by pull request 271 (squash d8981b0e00751c69247320085584e0939968043b) and five of them turned none of the 11 rows in api/tests/HpsmPoc.Api.Tests/Hosting/SqlServerWakeOpenRetryTests.cs red; these are gaps in the test rows, not defects found in the product code. Each is a change to api/src/HpsmPoc.Modules.Assessment/Persistence/SqlServerWakeRetry.cs. One: the scope check written as HandledRace.Active is null (line 28), which takes the retry away from keyed scopes; reachable in a wake, for example the first sign-in save inside HandledRace.Expect (Caller.cs line 110) and the self-customer save (CustomerEndpoints.cs line 150). Two: the sync ConnectionFailed override removed (lines 62-63). Three: AddOrUpdate changed to Add (lines 63 and 67), which throws when the same exception instance is marked twice. Four: the exact type check widened to is InvalidOperationException (line 56), which accepts subclasses. Five: the InnerException check dropped (line 56), which accepts a pool wait carrying an inner exception. The gate graded one, three, four and five minor, and two a note, because the sync hook is reached only by the start-up Database.Migrate (AssessmentModule.cs line 185) and no request read is sync. Nothing here is deployed.
- `<F2-1>` = Fix shape (the gate's): add a row with HandledRace.Expect(key) around a read whose first open times out at login (retried); a row feeding the same exception instance to two concurrent opens (both retried); rows with an ObjectDisposedException and with a pool-wait InvalidOperationException that carries an inner exception (neither retried). The gate names no row for the sync hook: pin it or record it as accepted. Test lines only; no product line changes. Done when: each of the five is pinned by a row that turns red under its named change, or is recorded as declined.
- `<F2-2>` = Provenance: gate report B1052 (its mutation table and findings) and builder report B1049, in 1_Project_Definition/Briefs/; the gate's cells are in the B1052 evidence folder, which is not copied to the analysis repository. Decision record: entry {C-271}. Related: HPSMPOC-428 and {KEY-F1}. Filed by records brief B1055, 2026-11-01. [REC-RES-PINS-01NOV-B1055]
